{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1554545-i-converted-viral-a-coc-modern-scenario-to-chronicles-of-darkness","id":1554545,"title":"I Converted Viral (a CoC Modern Scenario) to Chronicles of Darkness","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-10-21T11:16:41-07:00","id":1554545,"title":"I Converted Viral (a CoC Modern Scenario) to Chronicles of Darkness","content":"So Viral is a scenario for modern Call of Cthulhu about a bunch of ghost hunters live-streaming their exploration of an abandoned island so they can hit a million YouTube describers. Naturally, horror then ensues.<br /> <br /> I bought it basically the second I saw Seth Skorkowsky review it, and I think it seemed perfectly fitting for a base mortal Chronicles of Darkness game, so I'm taking that on. I like the system more than CoC. It's simpler to me, I like rolling tons of dice when I'm good at something, and the sanity mechanics don't seem that necessary for a campaign with this premise, while the vices and aspirations seem like a great addition, because they help incentivize the players to push the characters to act on their desire for fame and money to keep going and ignoring the omens and warning signs.<br /> <br /> First, quick plug. It's on twitch.tv/goodberrycafe this Saturday 7PM PST/9PM MT. Great cast, super excited. It's all to raise money for a friend's fundraiser to a bunch of actors, cosplayers, performers, who got defrauded (allegedly) by a convention they worked for and pay for legal aid to help them fight back.<br /> <br /> Okay anyway, here's what I'm doing so far. Wondering what people's thoughts on it are:<br /> <br /> <u>On Madness and Sanity</u><br /> I've run this once before and last time I made up a sanity system where you took sanity damage, directly taken from the CoC scenario when you failed a Breaking Point roll, and marked it with little tally marks on your sheet that applied penalties to breaking point rolls. Once you failed a breaking point roll, the sanity damage reset, but you'll still get future penalties as your Integrity lowers.<br /> <br /> This will be a 2-3 hour one-shot so I want to keep it as simplified as possible, so I think I'll throw that system away. Looking back, I may have been overthinking it, and the base Breaking Points and Integrity system will be fine. I'll just pair failing a Breaking Point roll with some CoC-style bouts of madness the scenario gives and it should be perfect, I think.<br /> <br /> <u>Beats</u><br /> Beats can be spent on regaining willpower or an automatic success on a contested roll. This is purely because it's a one-shot, not a CoC to CofD thing.<br /> <br /> <u>Conditions</u><br /> Think I'll simplify Conditions too for the same reason. I'm stealing the idea I've seen to make them Fate-like aspects that stick on you until you spend them to get a penalty to a roll or make your character act negatively in response to the condition. Then you get a beat. If it's a positive condition, you can spend it to get a +1 to a roll.<br /> <br /> Any thoughts on this? Do you think it'll work? Had anyone else tried anything like this before?<br /> <br /> I've done conversions of adventures from one system to another before, so don't think this will be too weird since it's modern horror to modern horror.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27512,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27512-next_raven","user":"Next_Raven","date":". 10-21-2025, 02:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27512-next_raven","name":"Next_Raven","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-21T11:26:51-07:00","id":1554547,"title":"","content":"Other things I'm considering I'd love to get people's thoughts on:<br /> <br /> <br /> I'm considering possibly letting Beats apply an automatic success on an investigation or perception roll, too, so you can automatically succeed on rolls to push the story forward, like in the Gumshoe system.<br /> <br /> For conditions, I'm also considering splitting them into two: like there are minor ones, like shaken or spooked, and bigger ones, like madness or frightened, something like that. And maybe the minor ones you can get by succeeding a breaking point roll, major one you get by failing, something like that.<br /> The minor one you resolve just like I said above, you give yourself a little penalty to a roll or do something dumb related to the condition. The bigger ones you have to resolve by voluntarily failing a roll, or giving yourself a dramatic failure from a normal failure. I think it's a cool idea, but not sure if that would over complicate things for a single one-shot, though.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27512-next_raven","name":"Next_Raven","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-22T14:43:46-07:00","id":1554564,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Next_Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1554545-i-converted-viral-a-coc-modern-scenario-to-chronicles-of-darkness?p=1554547#post1554547\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Other things I'm considering I'd love to get people's thoughts on:<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I think changing Beats for Willpower to Beats for Auto-success is a better choice for a one-shot, unless they give you Full Willpower and/or the characters have other uses for Willpower than getting extra dice/extra Defense.<br /> <br /> Having two possible uses makes things a bit too complex for a 2-3 hour game, especially since both uses do mostly the same thing, just with different rules. Extra Success vs + Dice is roughly the same average benefit, but the extra success will speed up things a little more.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, an equally good option is for Beats to be completely exchanged for immediate Willpower recover (1 or more, your call).<br /> <br /> The two types of Conditions seem too much. I think it may be a good alternative rule for an actual chronicle, if you feel the Conditions list is too much bookkeeping for your game, but for a one-shot it's adding too much layers that probably won't be used to full effect anyway.<br /> <br /> CoC and CoD have a lot of thematic overlap as far as it affects the system, and Integrity is already largely inspired by Sanity. I don't think having both systems will help, although fusing them for a longer game may be an option. But overall I think you have a solid idea, the scenario shouldn't be too hard to adapt and CoD will run smoothly for it. It will also be less volatile, which may be either a good or bad thing depending on what you want. In this case, it will make it more probable that most players reach the end of the story in either too good or too bad overall conditions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-23T00:08:23-07:00","id":1554587,"title":"","content":"Neat I never looked into CoC, and only dabbled in Delta Green, but I always thought some of their concepts would be easily ported over.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-23T01:03:16-07:00","id":1554588,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Next_Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1554545-i-converted-viral-a-coc-modern-scenario-to-chronicles-of-darkness#post1554545\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Had anyone else tried anything like this before?</div> </div> </div> </div>Me and my friends used to play 1e CofD with the CoC sanity system from 6e very loosely bolted on. I think it was based on Willpower*5 as a percentage, if I remember right (pretty harsh, but it functioned quite well).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-23T07:18:04-07:00","id":1554593,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1554545-i-converted-viral-a-coc-modern-scenario-to-chronicles-of-darkness?p=1554587#post1554587\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Neat I never looked into CoC, and only dabbled in Delta Green, but I always thought some of their concepts would be easily ported over.</div> </div> </div> </div>The system itself isn't anything special today. Not bad, just fairly generic (which was by design). Of course, a lot of <a href=\"https://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/SeinfeldIsUnfunny\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;Seinfeld&quot; Is Unfunny</a> applies.<br /> <br /> It's skill-focused, even more than CoD or WoD. The book has good advice on running investigations, as they're the main action in the game, but other than that what shines on it is the Sanity system. And the general deadliness, it makes running mortals in WoD seems forgiving.<br /> <br /> Of course, if you're interested on it as a piece of history, then you definitely should get your hands on a copy. It was the first big skill-based system (the BRP system), it introduced Sanity, it got a lot of awards on the games market, and it's the most influential literature on the Lovecraftian Mythos since the works of HPL's own literary executor, August Derleth. So this game is kind of a big deal, even if not an exceptional system.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-23T15:21:06-07:00","id":1554613,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1554545-i-converted-viral-a-coc-modern-scenario-to-chronicles-of-darkness?p=1554587#post1554587\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Neat I never looked into CoC, and only dabbled in Delta Green, but I always thought some of their concepts would be easily ported over.</div> </div> </div> </div>You know, I never really thought to until I saw this scenario. In my mind, CoC was always the 1920's gaslamp game and nWoD/CoD was always the modern horror game. But now that I discovered Modern Call of Cthulhu is a thing, and if this upcoming game goes well, I'll totally have to look at other scenarios like that.<br /> <br /> I haven't looked into Delta Green too much. I know you play as a military-like team doing missions and I think it uses a Call Of Cthulhu system of some sort. Is that like a Call of Cthulhu Modern game, too?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27512,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27512-next_raven","user":"Next_Raven","date":". 10-23-2025, 06:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27512-next_raven","name":"Next_Raven","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-23T15:35:05-07:00","id":1554615,"title":"","content":"As for porting, to be honest I am surprised how easy this has been. It seems to be porting over super easily. Basically the only complication is the Sanity system, and the magic/power system, but CoD basically has its own version of both those things with Breaking Points and Hunter/Second Sight, stuff like that, that I can't even say that has been much work.<br /> <br /> Most of my changes above were to adopt the system to a one-shot than CoC lol.<br /> <br /> For example, spoilers for one of the pregens: (can we spoiler tag stuff?)<br /> \u200b\u200bThere's a character here with psychic powers and it's pretty loosely goosey but they have a simple version of the system and a more crunchy version where they delineate a bunch of powers they might have. Well I basically took them and it easily mapped onto a style-like psychic power merit, 1 to 5 dots, that I gave to the player. How convenient! Lol<br /> <br /> Anyway, <br /> We'll see if I run into anything unexpected during this actual play, like if something in the book stumps me, but so far it's like it was made for this system lol. All the pregens had super easy to spot virtues, vices, and little commons habits or goals for the scenario that I turned into aspirations. Only thing I had to be kind of creative about was picking out merits that fit each character.\u200b And like I said, the sanity system stumped me for a sec, but I'm just going to try going with the standard Breaking Point system and see if it works. Just make it a little more common with how often I make those rolls maybe to match the whole descent into insanity thing they like so much.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27512-next_raven","name":"Next_Raven","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-23T15:43:07-07:00","id":1554617,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1554545-i-converted-viral-a-coc-modern-scenario-to-chronicles-of-darkness?p=1554564#post1554564\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think changing Beats for Willpower to Beats for Auto-success is a better choice for a one-shot, unless they give you Full Willpower and/or the characters have other uses for Willpower than getting extra dice/extra Defense.<br /> <br /> Having two possible uses makes things a bit too complex for a 2-3 hour game, especially since both uses do mostly the same thing, just with different rules. Extra Success vs + Dice is roughly the same average benefit, but the extra success will speed up things a little more.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, an equally good option is for Beats to be completely exchanged for immediate Willpower recover (1 or more, your call).<br /> <br /> The two types of Conditions seem too much. I think it may be a good alternative rule for an actual chronicle, if you feel the Conditions list is too much bookkeeping for your game, but for a one-shot it's adding too much layers that probably won't be used to full effect anyway.<br /> <br /> CoC and CoD have a lot of thematic overlap as far as it affects the system, and Integrity is already largely inspired by Sanity. I don't think having both systems will help, although fusing them for a longer game may be an option. But overall I think you have a solid idea, the scenario shouldn't be too hard to adapt and CoD will run smoothly for it. It will also be less volatile, which may be either a good or bad thing depending on what you want. In this case, it will make it more probable that most players reach the end of the story in either too good or too bad overall conditions.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for the insights! You make great points. I'm glad you responded because I'm going to change some things.<br /> <br /> I'm going to change the Beats to an automatic success so it only does one thing, and also I'll keep it to one type of simplified conditions. Would be cool if I got these players to play another chronicle with me one day and I could open it up to a bit more complication now that they'll be more familiar with the rules, but I won't hold my breath lol.<br /> <br /> I also think less volatile will be a good thing. Hopefully it keeps things slightly more predictable. This will be tight so we don't really have time for things to go off the rails until the very end.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27512-next_raven","name":"Next_Raven","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-23T19:47:46-07:00","id":1554631,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Next_Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1554545-i-converted-viral-a-coc-modern-scenario-to-chronicles-of-darkness?p=1554613#post1554613\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I haven't looked into Delta Green too much. I know you play as a military-like team doing missions and I think it uses a Call Of Cthulhu system of some sort. Is that like a Call of Cthulhu Modern game, too?</div> </div> </div> </div>Kind of that. It's one of the many, many games that licensed <i>Chaosium</i>'s CoC to do stuff. A lot of important games wioth Lovecraftian material did that because of their Sanity system and their take on the Mythos.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Next_Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1554545-i-converted-viral-a-coc-modern-scenario-to-chronicles-of-darkness?p=1554615#post1554615\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For example, spoilers for one of the pregens: (can we spoiler tag stuff?)</div> </div> </div> </div>You just have to code it, it's similar to the code you see on the text when you hit Quote.<br /> <br /> The code for spoiler is, in fact SPOILER. start with [ ], end with [/ ].<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Next_Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1554545-i-converted-viral-a-coc-modern-scenario-to-chronicles-of-darkness?p=1554615#post1554615\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">so far it's like it was made for this system lol</div> </div> </div> </div>In a sense it was, as CoC is the forefather of the Storyteller System. It also helps that CoC is based on a universal system, so it's rarely hard to parse unto anything.\u200b<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Next_Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1554545-i-converted-viral-a-coc-modern-scenario-to-chronicles-of-darkness?p=1554617#post1554617\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also think less volatile will be a good thing. Hopefully it keeps things slightly more predictable. This will be tight so we don't really have time for things to go off the rails until the very end.</div> </div> </div> </div>CoC is meant to go off the rails by design, although not in a way that slows the game. The basic expectation with it is that most (and I don't mean some, I mean <i><b>most</b></i>) PCs will either die horribly or go completely insane before the <i>session</i> ends.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her prono